      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- CIP\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n\n## Column Mapping\n- offer department code: SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- 2012SU term: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- total units: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- subject title: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- course number: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER\n- department name: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- dense rank: SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- course: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n- course description: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- school name: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME\n- program code: CIP.PROGRAM_CODE\n- program title: CIP.PROGRAM_TITLE\n- category code: CIP.CATEGORY_CODE\n- category title: CIP.CATEGORY_TITLE\n- four digit code: CIP.FOUR_DIGIT_CODE\n- four digit title: CIP.FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE\n- minimum warehouse load date: CIP.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\n- department 6: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT\n- total subjects: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- total courses: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- CIP.PROGRAM_CODE <-> SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. List the subject title from the subject summary, the course number from the subject offered summary, and the department name from the subject summary, along with dense ranks over the offer department code from the subject offered table, ordered by offer department code, for subjects in the 2012SU term and with total units greater than 0.\n```sql\nSELECT t2.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.COURSE_NUMBER, t2.DEPARTMENT_NAME, DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE ORDER BY t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE) AS window_column FROM SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY t0 JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2012SU' AND t2.TOTAL_UNITS > 0\n```\n2. For courses in the SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION table with a department code of 6, show the course, course description, department name, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group, ordered by category code.\n```sql\nSELECT s.COURSE, s.COURSE_DESCRIPTION, s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SCHOOL_NAME, c.PROGRAM_CODE, c.PROGRAM_TITLE, c.CATEGORY_CODE, c.CATEGORY_TITLE, c.FOUR_DIGIT_CODE, c.FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE, MIN(c.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE) OVER (PARTITION BY c.CATEGORY_CODE ORDER BY c.CATEGORY_CODE) AS min_warehouse_load_date FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION s JOIN CIP c ON c.PROGRAM_CODE = s.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE WHERE s.DEPARTMENT = 6\n```\n3. For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, and the dense rank over the offer department code, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code in the format (null, null, department name, null, total subjects).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t2.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.COURSE_NUMBER, t2.DEPARTMENT_NAME, DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE ORDER BY t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE) AS window_column FROM SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY t0 JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2012SU' AND t2.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 ) , dept_counts AS ( SELECT DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(*) AS total_subjects FROM SUBJECT_SUMMARY WHERE TERM_CODE = '2012SU' AND TOTAL_UNITS > 0 GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT ic.SUBJECT_TITLE, ic.COURSE_NUMBER, ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.window_column, NULL AS total_subjects FROM inner_cte ic UNION ALL SELECT NULL, NULL, dc.DEPARTMENT_NAME, NULL, dc.total_subjects FROM dept_counts dc ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUBJECT_TITLE\n```\n4. For courses in the SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION table with a department code of 6, show the course, course description, department name, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group, ordered by category code. Additionally, for each school name, include a grand total for all courses in that school in the format of (nulls for course-specific fields, school name, nulls for other fields, and the total number of courses in that school).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT s.COURSE, s.COURSE_DESCRIPTION, s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SCHOOL_NAME, c.PROGRAM_CODE, c.PROGRAM_TITLE, c.CATEGORY_CODE, c.CATEGORY_TITLE, c.FOUR_DIGIT_CODE, c.FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE, MIN(c.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE) OVER (PARTITION BY c.CATEGORY_CODE ORDER BY c.CATEGORY_CODE) AS min_warehouse_load_date FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION s JOIN CIP c ON c.PROGRAM_CODE = s.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE WHERE s.DEPARTMENT = 6 ), SchoolTotals AS ( SELECT NULL AS COURSE, NULL AS COURSE_DESCRIPTION, NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, NULL AS PROGRAM_CODE, NULL AS PROGRAM_TITLE, NULL AS CATEGORY_CODE, NULL AS CATEGORY_TITLE, NULL AS FOUR_DIGIT_CODE, NULL AS FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE, NULL AS min_warehouse_load_date, COUNT(*) AS total_courses FROM inner_cte GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME ) SELECT i.COURSE, i.COURSE_DESCRIPTION, i.DEPARTMENT_NAME, i.SCHOOL_NAME, i.PROGRAM_CODE, i.PROGRAM_TITLE, i.CATEGORY_CODE, i.CATEGORY_TITLE, i.FOUR_DIGIT_CODE, i.FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE, i.min_warehouse_load_date, NULL AS total_courses FROM inner_cte i UNION ALL SELECT s.COURSE, s.COURSE_DESCRIPTION, s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SCHOOL_NAME, s.PROGRAM_CODE, s.PROGRAM_TITLE, s.CATEGORY_CODE, s.CATEGORY_TITLE, s.FOUR_DIGIT_CODE, s.FOUR_DIGIT_TITLE, s.min_warehouse_load_date, s.total_courses FROM SchoolTotals s ORDER BY SCHOOL_NAME, CATEGORY_CODE, COURSE\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers."
